cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cited for the mandatory notAfter field and the 99991231235959Z 'no
  well-defined expiration' sentinel."
title: "Internet X.509 Public Key Infrastructure Certificate and Certificate
  Revocation List (CRL) Profile"
type: standard
authors:
  - name: "Cooper, D."
  - name: "Santesson, S."
  - name: "Farrell, S."
  - name: "Boeyen, S."
  - name: "Housley, R."
  - name: "Polk, W."
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.17487/RFC5280
  - type: other
    value: RFC 5280
url: "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5280#section-4.1.2.5"
date-released: 2008-05
license: "IETF Trust License"
notes: "§4.1.2.5: 'The validity period for a certificate is the period of time
  from notBefore through notAfter, inclusive. […] To indicate that a certificate
  has no well-defined expiration date, the notAfter SHOULD be assigned the
  GeneralizedTime value of 99991231235959Z.' RFD 2145 chooses NOT to use the
  sentinel because embedded and legacy X.509 parsers reject the year field."
